    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0488" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357. AK/5–2551: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States Mission at
                        the United Nations </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-05-29T20:00:00-04:00">May 29, 1951—8 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>953. Reurtel 1585, May 25, Dept has no objection and wld defer to GOC’s judgment
                    on advisability of GOC making a report to GA at this time. We have some
                    question, however, as to wisdom of supplementing report with draft res along the
                    lines indicated in reftel. We cannot see what such a res wld accomplish.</p>
                <p>As we have previously indicated (Deptel 925, May 14), we do not <pb facs="0489"
                        n="473" xml:id="pg473"/> consider a GA res the best vehicle for negotiating
                    peaceful settlement or cease-fire. Efforts to open negotiations leading to
                    termination of hostilities are far more likely to succeed if done discreetly
                    through GOC or available diplomatic channels and later confirmed by GA. Open
                    discussion in GA on such res with inevitable recriminations, propaganda and
                    face-saving, only make achievement cease-fire more difficult. Further, GA res
                    which wld be meaningful almost inevitably involves commitments by UC and UN
                    Members who will pay attention to GA res and none by the Commies, thus putting
                    the latter in a far better negotiating position.</p>
                <p>We suggest that GOC cld report its efforts to date and let report speak for
                    itself.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
